From 9b71491fc9554d2bfc49a921dc6a547a400ebc8b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Buckley <10402042+ryancbuckley@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 12:03:12 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] rustfmt built into rustc for WASI hosts (RUSTC_RUSTFMT=1)

As with Clippy, without dylibs a separate rustfmt would carry a second copy
of the compiler crates it uses. On WASI, rustc links rustfmt, and with
RUSTC_RUSTFMT set it is `rustfmt [--edition E] FILE...`, formatting the
files in place (compiler/rustc/src/rustfmt.rs). rustfmt gets Cargo
dependencies on the compiler crates it uses through extern crate, and,
built as a compiler crate, allows the lints that then apply to it.
---
 Cargo.lock                    | 12 +++++++
 compiler/rustc/Cargo.toml     |  2 ++
 compiler/rustc/src/main.rs    |  6 ++++
 compiler/rustc/src/rustfmt.rs | 61 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 src/tools/rustfmt/Cargo.toml  | 14 ++++++++
 src/tools/rustfmt/src/lib.rs  |  4 +++
 6 files changed, 99 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 compiler/rustc/src/rustfmt.rs

